hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18212","Abdullah said: I read to my father's book: Sufyan informed us, Mahdi ibn Jafar al-Ramli narrated to us, Abu al-Walid Rudayh ibn Atiyyah narrated to us from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, he said: I saw Abu Ubayy al-Ansari, and he is the son of Abu Haram al-Ansari, and he informed me that he prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) toward both qiblas, wearing a dusty cloak of khazz."
"18213","Kathir ibn Marwan Abu Muhammad narrated to us in the year one hundred eighty-one, Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, he said: I saw Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Umm Haram al-Ansari, and he had prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) toward both qiblas, wearing a dusty garment of khazz, and Ibrahim pointed with his hand to his shoulders, and Kathir thought it was a cloak."
